Here's TUnit's lifecycle at each scope:

---

## 1. Before/After Every Individual Test in a Class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public async Task ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        await InMemoryDb.ResetAsync();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public async Task Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        // runs after each test
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_IsValid() { /* ... */ }
}
```

You can also use the **constructor** (setup) and `IAsyncDisposable.DisposeAsync` (teardown).

---

## 2. Once Before/After All Tests in a Class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static async Task OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once before the first test in this class
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static async Task DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once after the last test in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_IsValid() { /* ... */ }
}
```

> `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` methods must be **static**.

---

## 3. Once Before/After All Tests in the Assembly

```csharp
public class GlobalAssemblyHooks
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StartWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // starts once before any test in this assembly
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StopWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // runs after every test in the assembly finishes
    }
}
```

---

## 4. Once for the Entire Test Session (cross-assembly)

```csharp
public class TestSessionHooks
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await Database.MigrateAsync();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDownDatabase(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await Database.DropAsync();
    }
}
```

---

## Global Cross-Cutting Hooks

Use `[BeforeEvery(Test)]` / `[AfterEvery(Test)]` (or the `Class`/`Assembly` variants) to run logic for **every** test across the entire run regardless of class:

```csharp
public class LoggingHooks
{
    [BeforeEvery(Test)]
    public static void LogStart(TestContext context)
        => Console.WriteLine($"Starting: {context.TestDetails.TestName}");
}
```

---

### Quick Reference

| Scope | Before | After |
|-------|--------|-------|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` / ctor | `[After(Test)]` / `Dispose` |
| Class | `[Before(Class)]` (static) | `[After(Class)]` (static) |
| Assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` (static) | `[After(Assembly)]` (static) |
| Session | `[Before(TestSession)]` (static) | `[After(TestSession)]` (static) |

All hooks optionally accept a context parameter and/or a `CancellationToken`.
